\f1\b \cf0 What is your primary goal as a filmmaker? (maximum 500 characters)\
\
My primary goal as a filmmaker is to use cinema as an "empathy machine" (Roger Ebert's term), connecting the audience to the hearts and minds of vivid, well realized characters. I frequently do this within the dark comedy and thriller genres, using them as a 'cry for help'; an examination of realistic characters trapped in surrealistic and/or extreme situations that society would often prefer not to talk about out loud about. Personal stories, told within viscerally satisfying genre frameworks. \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl380\ql\qnatural

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl380\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf0 Which directors work do you feel the strongest affinity with? Explain why. (maximum 500 Characters)\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri720\ql\qnatural
\cf0 I relate most strongly to the personal visions of Charlie Kaufman, David Lynch, The Coen Brothers and Martin Scorsese. All of these filmmakers have made exceptionally well crafted films within the dark comedy/thriller genres. Their work convincingly showcases relatable, vulnerable characters in high stakes psychological situations, leaving room for gallows humour along the way. These artists inspire me to be bold, thoughtful, daring and honest, and their worldview seems very similar to mine. \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl380\ql\qnatural

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl380\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf0 What are your top 3 favourite films and why? (maximum 500 Characters)\
\
Synecdoche New York, Bad Boy Bubby and Taxi Driver all display enormous empathy and concentrated subjectivity for lonely, complex, misunderstood characters. Each film also transcends its exploitation / genre roots with their bold personal statements; even Synecdoche New York was Kaufman's attempt to make a horror film as per his for-hire assignment. The surreal, expressionistic elements add to each film's rewatchability and timelessness.  \
\
\
