Description of clip (250 words) - Artless \
Artless is a complete public service announcement I directed about impending arts cuts in British Columbia. The intended use was to tell a story that spread an urgent and powerful message in a poetic way. The result was a premiere at the Wrecking Ball Festival, a viral video campaign, screenings in educational institutions, a month long run at the Vancity Theatre, and numerous press articles that brought the dystopian tale to a wider audience. \
\
\
Why did you choose this clip (250 words) \
\
Artless is a strong example of my visual storytelling as a director, and working with an actor who can speak volumes without saying a word. I used a grey rectangle, the symbol used by the protest movement at the time, as a replacement image for art in Vancouver cultural spaces. These former institutions for art included an art gallery, library, movie theatre and classical music stage. The resulting lack of artistic inspiration gives the young spectator no arts or culture institutions to be nourished by, leading to him drawing only the same symbol he sees everywhere around him.\
